# Agno Content Pipeline in OSOP Format

osop_version: "1.0"

id: agno-content-pipeline

name: Agno Content Pipeline Workflow

description: A multi-step content creation pipeline — research a topic, plan an outline, write a draft, review it, then publish. Demonstrates Agno Agent and Workflow patterns in a portable, tool-agnostic format.

tags: [agno, agent, workflow, content, pipeline]

nodes:
  - id: user-request
    type: human
    name: User Request
    description: User provides a topic for the content piece.

  - id: research
    type: agent
    name: Research Agent
    description: Searches the web for current information, statistics, and sources on the topic.
    runtime:
      provider: openai
      model: gpt-5.6-luna
    config:
      tools: [web_search]
      temperature: 0.3

  - id: plan
    type: agent
    name: Content Planner
    description: Turns research findings into a structured outline with sections and key points.
    runtime:
      provider: openai
      model: gpt-5.6-luna
    config:
      temperature: 0.5

  - id: write
    type: agent
    name: Writer Agent
    description: Writes the full content draft following the outline.
    runtime:
      provider: openai
      model: gpt-5.6-luna
    config:
      temperature: 0.7

  - id: review
    type: agent
    name: Reviewer Agent
    description: Reviews the draft for accuracy, tone, and structure, and produces the final version.
    runtime:
      provider: openai
      model: gpt-5.6-luna
    config:
      temperature: 0.2

  - id: publish
    type: api
    name: Publish Content
    description: Deliver the final content (save to file or hand off to a publishing API).

edges:
  - from: user-request
    to: research
    mode: sequential

  - from: research
    to: plan
    mode: sequential

  - from: plan
    to: write
    mode: sequential

  - from: write
    to: review
    mode: sequential

  - from: review
    to: publish
    mode: sequential
